title: Military Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: military_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: lwusp_in_government = 1 and defense_minister_party = "LWUSP" and military_policy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/kruger.jpg
#subtitle: Dealing with the Sordish Armed Forces.

= Military Policy

The Army is a deeply <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> institution that has been generally hostile to any notion of democracy. They also have a history of involvement in civilian matters since the times of the Civil War. However, we now control the military as part of the government. What should we do to reform it?

- @increase_funding: Increase funding for the military to purchase its loyalty.
- @decrease_funding: Reduce funding for the military so we have more for social spending.
- @reform: Conduct a thorough reform of the ranks, reducing the influence of <span style="color: #6e377a;">Sollists</span> and making it more hospitable to us.
- @modernize: Modernize the military
- @expand: Expand the military
- @root: No change to military policy.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@increase_funding
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0 and in_usp_coalition; army_loyalty += 0.07 if army_loyalty < 1; army_strength += 20; left_dissent += 5; rumburg_relation -= 1; rwusp_relation += 4; nfp_relation += 4; cwusp_relation += 2; economic_growth += 0.1; coup_progress -= 1; military_funding += 1

The military and right-wing parties are pleasantly surprised that we would increase military funding. As the threat of Rumburg becomes more and more real with every day that passes, the military starts looking like a valid investment.

@decrease_funding
subtitle: +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: army_strength > 0
on-arrival: budget += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_usp_coalition; rwusp_relation -= 8; cwusp_relation -= 4; nfp_relation -= 6; army_militancy -= 1; army_strength -= 20; ys_strength += 15; bff_strength += 5; ys_militancy += 0.05; army_loyalty -= 0.05 if army_loyalty > 0; coup_progress += 2; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty < 0.2; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty < 0.1; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty <= 0; economic_growth -= 0.1; military_funding -= 1

The military has fewer guns and fewer soldiers. There is no hint of a coup yet, but we do not know where the line will be drawn. The right-wing parties are committed to the military and deeply opposed to our budget cuts.

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1 and army_loyalty < 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the budget. ?][? if army_loyalty >= 1 : The Army is already fully loyal to the democratic government. ?]
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1 if in_usp_coalition; army_loyalty += 0.15; army_militancy -= 0.5 if army_loyalty < 0.5; budget -= 1; coup_progress += 1; rwusp_relation -= 5; pacifism += 1; democratization += 1;

Our efforts are at least somewhat successful; we have changed the recruiting and training patterns so that more soldiers from non-<span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> backgrounds can join, hopefully changing the culture of the forces. We have also removed some of the officers who supported Eduard Luderin during the Civil War.

The right-wing parties are committed to the military and deeply suspicious of our efforts to reform it.

@modernize
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
view-if: military_expansion = 0
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: military_modernization += 1; army_militancy += 1; army_strength -= 20; budget -= 1
go-to: modernize_what

The Sordish Armed Forces are very old-fashioned and backwards, both in their equipment and in their tactics. We shall change that and modernize the army to bring it on par with the rest of the world.

@modernize_what

What do we wish to modernize?

- @modernize_army: Modernize the Army
- @modernize_navy: Modernize the Navy
- @modernize_airforce: Modernize the Air Force

@modernize_army
on-arrival: modernized_army += 1; army_strength += 30

We have modernized the Army.

@modernize_navy
on-arrival: modernized_navy += 1; economic_growth += 0.1; army_strength += 10

We have modernized the Navy.

@modernize_airforce
on-arrival: modernized_airforce += 1; army_strength += 20

We have modernized the Air Force.

@expand
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
view-if: military_modernization = 0
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: military_expansion += 1; army_strength += 20; budget -= 1
go-to: expand_what

The Sordish Armed Forces obviously need more soldiers to deal with the growing threat of Rumburg.

@expand_what

What do we wish to expand?

- @expand_army: Expand the Army
- @expand_navy: Expand the Navy
- @expand_airforce: Expand the Air Force

@expand_army
on-arrival: expanded_army += 1; army_strength += 50

We have expanded the Army.

@expand_navy
on-arrival: expanded_navy += 1; economic_growth += 0.1; army_strength += 20

We have expanded the Navy.

@expand_airforce
on-arrival: expanded_airforce += 1; army_strength += 40

We have expanded the Air Force
